"note_claim": "Caustic soda reacts violently with water, potentially causing the solution to boil, splatter, or explode and causing severe burns.",
"label": "SUPPORTS",
"quote": "Caustic soda is exothermic when it is combined with water or acids, giving off a tremendous amount of heat. When the reaction is not properly controlled, it will make the solution boil, splatter, or even explode",
"reason": "The page explicitly states that mixing caustic soda with water can cause boiling, splattering, or exploding and result in burn hazards."
